- op: discuss  # 4359
  at: '2026-07-30T19:50:58Z'  # 4359
  by: agent  # 4359
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4359
  clock: 5  # 4359
  nonce: '4359'  # 4359
  message: "DONE — PR #92 merged, dev 6aaa44070d. (Supersedes the LEFT-OPEN note above: the CI failure was diagnosed and fixed once the owner supplied the log.)\n\nTHE CI FAILURE WAS NOT IN THIS CHANGE. It was 'docs/ARCHITECTURE.md is out of date: generated 17 commits ago, exceeds the 15-commit window'. I had pre-flighted all five verify-generated --check gates green BEFORE pushing — but auto-pr then REBASED the branch onto a dev that had advanced (a tracker auto-sync plus the WI-gapir merge), and that check keys on commit-count DISTANCE, so the window moved underneath the pre-flight. Regenerating ARCHITECTURE.md on the rebased branch turned CI green on the next run with no change to the fix itself.\n\nDURABLE, and worth adding to the standing guidance: 'pre-flight the verify-generated gates before every auto-pr' (register pt.30) is NECESSARY BUT NOT SUFFICIENT — auto-pr's own rebase invalidates the pre-flight whenever dev moves between pre-flight and push, which a tracker auto-sync makes routine. The reliable form is to re-check AFTER the rebase, or to treat a regen as the first recovery step on any verify-generated CI failure.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED:\n(a) The asymmetry fix. finalize._finalize_skipped_into_limits keyed only on a run's files_skipped, so a parse-error drop set limits.partial_results_reason while an oversize drop — which lands only in limits.truncated_files, since add_truncated_file never touches files_skipped — set nothing. Two equivalent soft drops, one signalled and one silent. It now triggers on EITHER channel, with a non-vacuity control asserting the reason stays empty when nothing was dropped.\n(b) The spec fix. See the adjudication below.\n(c) Three tests: each channel plus the no-drops control.\n\nTHE ADJUDICATION (the substantive finding). The item's second half — 'analysis_incomplete never trips' — is CORRECT BEHAVIOUR and was deliberately NOT changed. My first implementation bound the flag to the reason so the rule the item quotes ('partial_results_reason present only when analysis_incomplete: true') would hold; it passed its tests and was WRONG. The spec's green-marked Analyzer-crashes section prescribes setting partial_results_reason AND states analysis_incomplete is not set, and the flag's own definition is 'terminated EARLY' while every fail-open drop explicitly continues. So the quoted constraint forbade a state the spec elsewhere mandates — NO implementation could satisfy both. That is a SPEC SELF-CONTRADICTION, not a code defect; the constraint was removed from the spec instead.\n\nGENERALIZABLE: when an item quotes a spec rule as violated, read every OTHER passage governing the same field before picking a side — the quoted one may be the defect.\n\nEvidence: 1598 passed across the 36-file affected set; finalize.py 100% under it; CI green."  # 4359
